"""Tank Wars development product, privacy and support pages."""
from pathlib import Path
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def build(page):
 base='/assets/apps/tank-wars/'
 body=f'''<style>.tank-hero{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2rem;align-items:center}}.tank-hero img{{width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:24px}}.tank-gallery{{display:grid;gap:1.2rem}}.tank-gallery img{{width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:18px}}.tank-gallery figure{{margin:0}}@media(max-width:650px){{.tank-hero{{grid-template-columns:1fr}}}}</style><section class="catalog-hero tank-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Android artillery game · Coming soon</p><h1>Tank Wars</h1><p class="lead">Aim high. Change the ground.</p><p>Line up your angle, choose your power and send a shell across the hills. Every crater changes the battlefield—and your next shot.</p><p><a class="button" href="#screenshots">See the battlefield</a> · <a href="/tank-wars/support/">How to play</a></p><p>In development. Not yet available on Google Play.</p></div><img src="{base}art.webp" width="768" height="768" alt="Forest-green and desert-tan camouflage tanks on opposing green hills beneath a golden shell arc"></section><section><h2>Make every shot count</h2><p>Tank Wars is a native Android, turn-based artillery game. Adjust your turret angle and firing power, watch the wind, then fire. Projectiles follow curved trajectories, explosions carve away terrain, and tanks fall when the ground underneath them disappears.</p><h2>Three ways to play</h2><p>Practice against the computer, trade turns with a friend on one phone or tablet, or try the paired Bluetooth Host a game / Join a game mode. Local gameplay needs no internet and no account.</p><p>Bluetooth is implemented in the development build, with the host calculating shots, damage and turns. Synchronization is tested in software; two-device radio gameplay still requires validation. Both devices need Bluetooth enabled, Android pairing and the same app version.</p><h2>A different battlefield</h2><p>Battle across rolling hills, ridgelines, trenches, border walls and fortified outposts. Tanks start farther apart on flat firing positions. Concrete defenses block shells and break down under explosions, so the battlefield changes with every hit.</p><h2>Choose your weapon</h2><p><strong>Shell</strong> gives you unlimited standard shots. <strong>Heavy</strong> makes a wider blast, with three rounds per battle. <strong>Drill</strong> digs deeper into the ground, also with three rounds. The illustrated weapon chooser shows your equipped shell and remaining ammunition. Use terrain damage to change your opponent’s position, but protect your own foothold.</p></section><section id="screenshots"><h2>Inside the game</h2><p>Actual Android development-build captures from the emulator. Final release details may change.</p><div class="tank-gallery"><figure><img src="{base}home.webp" width="2400" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Tank Wars landscape menu with computer, two-player and Bluetooth modes"><figcaption>Choose a battle. Settings uses the gear icon.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="{base}game.webp" width="2400" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Tank Wars battlefield with terrain, tanks, aiming sliders and Fire button"><figcaption>Native touch controls and a Canvas-rendered battlefield.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section><h2>Play at your pace</h2><p>Pause mid-shot, then resume where you left off. Local battles save on your device. Sound is optional. Compact controls keep the battlefield visible on phones and tablets.</p><h2>Between battles</h2><p>Tank Wars is planned as a free, ad-supported game with no purchases or subscriptions. Players under 18 and those who do not specify an age play without ads. Adults may receive non-personalized, G-rated ad requests after privacy checks, only after a completed battle when starting another battle or returning Home. Dismiss the ad to continue; if none is ready, continue immediately. Local gameplay works offline. Production advertising remains disabled in the current candidate pending approval and physical-device verification.</p></section><p><a href="/tank-wars/privacy/">Privacy policy</a> · <a href="/tank-wars/support/">Support</a></p>'''
 page('/tank-wars/','Tank Wars — Android Artillery Game','Aim, fire and reshape the hills in Tank Wars for Android. Turn-based artillery, destructible terrain, three weapons and offline local play. Coming soon.',body,'https://tripperdeelabs.com'+base+'art.webp')
 page('/tank-wars/privacy/','Tank Wars privacy policy','Tank Wars age choices, local saves, optional Bluetooth and privacy-gated advertising.','''<section><h1>Tank Wars privacy policy</h1><p>Updated November 7, 2026. This describes Tank Wars 0.4.0, the current Android candidate, package com.tripperdeelabs.tankwars, provided by TripperDeeLabs.</p><h2>Local battle data</h2><p>Age-group choice, terrain, tank health, turn, projectile state and sound preferences are saved in the app’s private device storage. No TripperDeeLabs account or cloud-save service is used. Uninstalling or clearing storage removes this data. Android backup is disabled in the manifest; manufacturer device-transfer behavior may vary.</p><h2>Bluetooth play</h2><p>Optional Bluetooth shares aiming and firing commands, terrain changes and battle state directly with your paired opponent. Android Nearby devices permission is requested on supported versions. The game uses Android settings for device discovery and pairing. Battle messages are not uploaded to a TripperDeeLabs server. Leaving the app ends the Bluetooth session; your separate local save is retained.</p><h2>Age groups and advertising</h2><p>The intended launch model is free with between-battle ads and no purchases. A neutral age-group selection asks for an age range, not a name or birth date. The choice stays in local app storage and can be changed in Settings. It is self-declared, not identity or parental verification. Gameplay is available for every selection.</p><p>Players under 18, those who prefer not to say, and invalid or missing age choices receive no ads. The app does not initiate UMP consent requests or initialize/request Mobile Ads for those groups. Child-directed and under-age request protections are set defensively. Changing from adult to a protected group discards pending ads and prevents new requests; it cannot undo data already processed during earlier adult use.</p><p>For adults, the ad-enabled implementation uses Google User Messaging Platform (UMP) to obtain applicable privacy choices before initializing Google Mobile Ads or requesting an ad. Each launch requires a successful privacy update; errors, missing setup, or disallowed requests keep ads off. Settings provides Ad privacy to revisit available privacy choices or retry. No consent form is intentionally displayed over active gameplay.</p><p>All ad requests are non-personalized, request maximum content rating G, and enable Google restricted data processing. UMP privacy signals still apply: non-personalized ads can still use device storage and process data. Ads can appear only when leaving a completed battle for New battle or Home. Unavailable ads never block continuing.</p><h2>Current candidate and SDK data</h2><p>Production advertising remains disabled by a separate build switch in the signed 0.4.0 candidate. Review builds use Google demonstration interstitials after the same age and privacy gates. Consent setup, device verification and owner approval are required before production advertising is activated.</p><p>When these SDK flows are used, Google may process IP addresses (which can imply approximate location), privacy choices, app/ad interactions, diagnostics and permitted device identifiers for consent, ad delivery, measurement and fraud prevention. Android Advertising ID and AdServices advertising ID, attribution and topics permissions are removed. App measurement initialization is delayed until the guarded SDK initialization. These restrictions do not establish that every SDK component collects no data. There is no developer-operated analytics backend or gameplay server.</p><p>See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/android/privacy/play-data-disclosure">Google’s SDK disclosure</a>. Clearing local storage removes local choices and saves; it does not delete data Google has already received. Google’s handling and retention follow its policies. No universal legal-compliance, Families eligibility or Play approval claim is made.</p><h2>Permissions and choices</h2><p>Internet/network-state access supports ads. Nearby devices access is optional for local play. Tank Wars does not request location, contacts, microphone or camera permission. There are no purchases in this build.</p><h2>Support and privacy questions</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com">tripperdeelabs@gmail.com</a>. We receive the information you choose to send and use it to respond. Avoid sending passwords or payment details. You may also contact us concerning support correspondence.</p><p>Website analytics are separate from the app and covered by our <a href="/privacy/">website privacy policy</a>.</p><p><a href="/tank-wars/">Game overview</a> · <a href="/tank-wars/support/">Support</a></p></section>''')
 page('/tank-wars/support/','Tank Wars support','How to aim, use weapons, pause, save and connect over Bluetooth in Tank Wars.','''<section><h1>Tank Wars support</h1><h2>Aim and fire</h2><p>Play in landscape. Move the Aim slider to change your turret angle and the Power slider to change shot strength. Tap the weapon name to choose Shell, Heavy or Drill. Tap FIRE when it is your turn. Drag across the battlefield to aim, or use the sliders for finer adjustments. A short dotted guide shows the initial wind-aware trajectory; each tank remembers its previous angle and power. Wind bends the trajectory. The turn passes after the shot and any falling tanks have settled.</p><h2>Win the battle</h2><p>Reduce the other tank’s health to zero. Nearby explosions damage tanks; falling can cause additional damage. Shell is unlimited, while Heavy and Drill each start with three rounds. Heavy creates a wider blast; Drill digs deeper. Two players takes turns on the same device; Play computer gives you a computer opponent.</p><h2>Pause and resume</h2><p>The two-bar icon pauses. Resume continues a shot or settling terrain. Home keeps the local battle, including ammunition and terrain. Starting a different local battle asks before replacing it. The gear opens Settings; the Home icon returns to the menu. Do not clear storage or uninstall to troubleshoot if you want to keep your save.</p><h2>Bluetooth setup</h2><p>Enable Bluetooth and pair both devices in Android Bluetooth settings. Install the same Tank Wars version on both. Choose Bluetooth play, then Host a game on one phone and Join a game on the other. Grant Nearby devices permission and select the hosting phone. The host controls the simulation; each player can aim and fire only on their own turn. Leaving the foreground disconnects the session. Reconnect to start a new battle. Two-device radio behavior is still being validated.</p><h2>Ads</h2><p>Players under 18 or with unknown age play without ads. Adults can use Settings → Ad privacy to review available choices or retry a failed privacy check. When approved and enabled, ads are non-personalized and appear only after a completed battle, on New battle or Home. Close the ad to continue; no ready ad means continue immediately. This signed candidate keeps production advertising disabled. Review builds use demo ads and still require privacy setup. Bluetooth sessions close before advertising; host and join again for another battle.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com?subject=Tank%20Wars%20support">tripperdeelabs@gmail.com</a> with your app version, device model and what happened.</p><p><a href="/tank-wars/">Game overview</a> · <a href="/tank-wars/privacy/">Privacy policy</a></p></section>''')
 home=ROOT/'index.html';soup=BeautifulSoup(home.read_text(),'html.parser');listing=soup.select_one('#in-development .app-directory');assert listing is not None
 listing.insert(0,BeautifulSoup(f'<li><a class="directory-preview" href="/tank-wars/"><img src="{base}home.webp" width="2400" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Tank Wars menu"></a><div class="directory-copy"><h3><a href="/tank-wars/">Tank Wars</a></h3><p class="availability">Coming soon</p><p>Aim, fire and reshape the hills in a turn-based Android artillery game with local play and three weapons.</p><p><a href="/tank-wars/">Explore the game</a> · <a href="/tank-wars/privacy/">Privacy</a></p></div></li>','html.parser').li);home.write_text(str(soup))
